<section class="faq-page section-spacing">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="faq-header reveal">
      <h1 class="faq-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
      <p class="faq-subtitle">Everything you need to know about our miners, shipping, and support.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-sections">
      <div class="faq-section reveal">
        <h2 class="faq-section-title">Mining Basics</h2>
        <div class="faq-group">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>What is ASIC mining?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>ASIC (Application-Specific Integrated Circuit) miners are specialized hardware designed to mine specific cryptocurrencies like Bitcoin. They're far more efficient than GPUs for SHA-256 mining.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>What's the difference between hashrate models?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Higher hashrate (TH/s) means more mining power. An S19 Pro 110TH mines faster than an S17 Pro 53TH, but also consumes more power. Efficiency (J/TH) matters too.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-section reveal">
        <h2 class="faq-section-title">ASIC Setup</h2>
        <div class="faq-group">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>How do I set up my ASIC miner?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Connect the PSU, plug in ethernet, power on, and access the miner's IP via your browser. Configure your pool settings and you're mining. Full setup guides included with purchase.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>What power supply do I need?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Most S19 series miners require an APW12 or equivalent PSU (3250W+). Check the product page for specific requirements. We sell compatible PSUs separately.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-section reveal">
        <h2 class="faq-section-title">Firmware & Tuning</h2>
        <div class="faq-group">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>What's the difference between Vnish and Braiins OS?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Both are custom firmware that replace stock firmware. Vnish offers overclocking features, while Braiins focuses on efficiency and stability. Both are pre-configured options we offer.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Can I tune my miner for efficiency?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes! Custom firmware allows tuning profiles for efficiency (lower power) or performance (higher hashrate). Our engineers can help configure optimal settings.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-section reveal">
        <h2 class="faq-section-title">Shipping & Warranty</h2>
        <div class="faq-group">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>How fast do you ship?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Most orders ship within 48 hours from our USA warehouse. Freight shipping takes 3-5 business days domestically. Tracking provided for all shipments.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>What warranty do you offer?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>All units include a 30-day warranty covering DOA and manufacturing defects. Extended warranty options available for wholesale orders.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Do you ship internationally?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Currently we ship within the USA only. International shipping may be available for large wholesale orders — contact sales for details.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-section reveal">
        <h2 class="faq-section-title">Power & Infrastructure</h2>
        <div class="faq-group">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>What electrical requirements do I need?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>You'll need 220-240V power circuits with adequate amperage (typically 15-20A per miner). Consult an electrician for facility-scale deployments.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>How loud are these miners?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>ASIC miners are loud (70-80dB). Not suitable for residential use. You'll need a dedicated space with proper ventilation and noise isolation.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-section reveal">
        <h2 class="faq-section-title">Wholesale Orders</h2>
        <div class="faq-group">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>What's the minimum for wholesale pricing?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Wholesale pricing starts at 10+ units. Pallet quantities (40-50 units) receive the best pricing. Contact sales for custom quotes.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Can you help with facility deployments?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes! We offer deployment consulting, firmware configuration, and ongoing support for facility-scale operations. Talk to our engineering team.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-cta reveal">
      <div class="faq-cta-card glass">
        <h2>Didn't find your answer?</h2>
        <p>Our team is here to help with any questions about hardware, setup, or wholesale orders.</p>
        <a href="/pages/contact" class="btn btn-premium">Contact Support</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

